course: dictionary
lesson: 4648
title: Historically: the past and true to history
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Historically is a word about time. It means in the past, or over a long period of history. «Historically, girls were not allowed to go to school.» The word Historically at the start tells you this rule was true long ago, not now.
explain: The word can also mean true to history. «Historically accurate» describes a film, story or picture where the details match the real past. If a film set in Roman times shows real clothes and real buildings, it is historically accurate.
explain: Look at the sentence around the word to find which meaning it has. In «It was reported that a big company's image generator made historically wrong pictures», the pictures were wrong about the real past, so the word means true to history. Check by swapping in "in the past" or "about history" and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Historically is an adverb: it tells you about when or how something happened.
fact: Meaning 1: historically means in the past, or over a long period of time.
fact: Meaning 2: historically means connected with history, or true to history.
fact: «Historically accurate» means true to the real past, with the right details.
fact: «Historically important» means important in history.
exercise: «Historically, girls were not allowed to go to school.» What does historically mean here? | Very quickly | In the future | *In the past, over a long time | Only today
exercise: A film set in Roman times has real clothes and real buildings, and the makers got every detail right. Which phrase describes the film? | *Historically accurate | Historically cold | Historically loud | Historically silly
exercise: In «made historically wrong pictures», what does historically mean? | Wrong in colour | Wrong about the weather | Wrong in size | *Wrong about the real past
test: What does «historically important» mean? | Important only today | Quite small | *Important in history | Very cheap
test: Which sentence uses historically to mean over a long period? | *Historically, most homes had no electricity. | I am historically hungry at lunch. | Dogs can swim fast. | The shop opened at nine.
exam: Maya says, «The tower is historically accurate», so what does she mean? | The tower is old and broken, and nobody knows why | The tower is very tall | The tower is painted red | *The tower looks exactly as it did in the past
